  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="AT3G16785-CPLX" textLabel="AT3G16785-CPLX" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G16785-CPLX" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="335" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>PLD zeta is the only Ca&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt; independent PLD isoform. It however requires PIP2 for activity.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G16785-CPLX" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="PLD &amp;zeta;" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="PLD" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="PLD zeta" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT3G16785-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-1793" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation__11891260_" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="AT3G15730-CPLX" textLabel="AT3G15730-CPLX" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G15730-CPLX" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="335" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>Five isoforms of phospholipase D, alpha, beta, gamma, delta, and zeta, have been reported and their catalytic activities have been demonstrated in E.coli. These isoforms are classified based upon their requirements of Ca&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt; for activity, dependence on phosphotidyl-4,5-bisphosphate (PIP2), and dependence on other phospholipids for activity. PLD&amp;alpha; requires milimolar Ca&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;, is PIP2-independent, and does not require binding of other phospholipids for activity. Its highest activity was detected in the plasma membrane.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G15730-CPLX" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="PLD &amp;alpha;" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="PLD" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="PLD alpha" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT3G15730-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-1789" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0016020" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCO-MEMBRANE" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation__10198096_" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation__11891260_" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation__WANG99_" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="AT4G11850-CPLX" textLabel="AT4G11850-CPLX" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G11850-CPLX" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="335" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>The enzyme activity of PLD gamma was detected in the plasma membrane, intracellular membrane, clathrin-coated vesicles, mitochondria, and nuclei. Its highest activity was found in old, senescing leaves.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G11850-CPLX" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="PLD &amp;gamma;" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="PLD" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="PLD gamma" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT4G11850-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-1791" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation__10198096_" />
